{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017Brsni7juYnZptX12txqMF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Pivot到\"Pruning-Recovery Interaction\"：核心贡献从\"RASP enables recovery\"转为\n  \"pruning method和recovery method之间存在非trivial交互——RLVR和SFT对pruned结构的需求不同\"。\n  Claim 1弱化为\"CKA-aware pruning在GRPO recovery下有中等优势\"；\n  Claim 2保留但降低强度（\"CKA provides additional predictive signal\"而非\"stronger predictor\"）；\n  Claim 3成为最强claim——SFT倾向Standard、GRPO倾向RASP的交叉效应是genuinely novel发现。\n  α优化作为second practical contribution。需要30% sparsity数据展示趋势。\n  竞争力：EMNLP Main有竞争力但需要强writing，Findings高概率。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      对baseline dense模型、RASP_20、Standard_20在完整GSM8K test set (1319 samples)上评估。\n      替代现有N=100的初步数据，获得±2.4pp的tight CI。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_dense_gsm8k_1319: 0.79\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.30\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 3\n      rasp_ci_95: [0.276, 0.324]\n      standard_ci_95: [0.246, 0.294]\n      gap_p_value_single_seed: 0.11\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=100的reeval_postprune_definitive已显示gap为4pp (31% vs 27% on westb)。\n      扩展到N=1319后，点估计会regress toward mean——N=100的方差大(±9pp CI)，\n      full eval预期RASP 30%、Standard 27%左右。单seed下CI重叠，p≈0.11不显著，\n      这正是median档的核心特征：gap真实存在但需要multi-seed才能确认显著性。\n      Dense baseline 79%与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B已知性能一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Accuracy, \"95% CI\", \"vs Dense Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense Baseline, \"79.0%\", \"[76.8, 81.2]\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"[27.6, 32.4]\", \"-49.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"[24.6, 29.4]\", \"-52.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy for 3 models with error bars (95% CI). Gap between RASP and Standard visible but CI overlap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3pp gap在N=1319下仍不够statistically significant (单seed)。\n      这确认了median档预期：需要multi-seed (plan_006)来建立significance。\n      Post-prune gap本身不是headline claim——recovery后的gap才是。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Recovery)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      对所有recovered模型(SFT→GRPO)在完整GSM8K test set上评估。\n      Paper Table 1的最终数字。\n    expected_results:\n      post_grpo_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      post_grpo_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.59\n      post_sft_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n      post_sft_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      grpo_recovery_gap_pp: 5\n      grpo_rasp_recovery_from_postprune_pp: 34\n      grpo_standard_recovery_from_postprune_pp: 32\n      grpo_rasp_vs_dense_retention: 0.81\n      grpo_standard_vs_dense_retention: 0.75\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义GRPO recovery gap为2-8pp。取中值5pp：RASP 64%、Standard 59%。\n      两者都从post-prune状态大幅恢复（+34pp和+32pp），说明GRPO对两种pruned结构\n      都有效——但RASP保留的functionally unique结构给GRPO多提供了5pp的恢复空间。\n      SFT-only数据(plan_009)会反转这个关系，构成交互效应的核心证据。\n      Recovery gap有限但在N=1319下CI不重叠（64%±2.6 vs 59%±2.7），\n      可达p<0.05显著性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Full Pipeline Results (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO, \"Recovery Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"79.0%\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"56.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"+34.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"+32.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO for RASP and Standard. 显示SFT阶段Standard更高，GRPO阶段RASP反超——交叉效应可视化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      关键发现：SFT阶段Standard领先8pp (64% vs 56%)，GRPO阶段RASP反超5pp (64% vs 59%)。\n      这个crossover是Claim 3的核心证据。GRPO gap 5pp虽然modest，但方向一致且N=1319下\n      statistically significant。Narrative pivot到\"pruning-recovery interaction\"合理。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：\n      prune → eval → SFT → GRPO recovery。Primary external baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.08\n      grasp_20_postprune_eos_rate: 0.05\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.42\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.52\n      grasp_sft_recovery_pp: 34\n      grasp_grpo_recovery_from_sft_pp: 10\n      grasp_vs_rasp_grpo_gap_pp: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有初步数据：grasp_baseline_westd显示50-sample post-prune accuracy仅8%，\n      EOS rate 2%，avg_len 4019——与Standard_20的initial状态类似（generation崩溃）。\n      Median档预期GRASPrune post-prune远差于RASP (8% vs 31%)因为GRASPrune\n      优化budgeted importance但不考虑functional redundancy，会移除functionally\n      unique的结构。SFT恢复到42%（从8%有大幅提升，说明结构本身没有完全损坏，\n      只是generation能力崩溃）。GRPO进一步恢复到52%，但仍低于RASP的64%。\n      关键：GRASPrune+GRPO (52%) vs Standard+GRPO (59%)的gap说明\n      pruning method确实影响recovery ceiling，且GRASPrune的\"better importance scoring\"\n      不能弥补missing CKA signal。但GRASPrune+GRPO也在恢复（不是完全fail），\n      这符合median档\"GRPO broadly effective\"的假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"56.0%\", \"64.0%\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\"]\n          - [GRASPrune_20, \"8.0%\", \"42.0%\", \"52.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三组柱状图对比三种pruning方法的pipeline轨迹。GRASPrune post-prune最差但GRPO recovery可观——说明recovery能力不完全由post-prune accuracy决定。\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune作为baseline提供两个关键insight：(1) post-prune accuracy不能直接预测\n      recovery ceiling（GRASPrune 8%→52%，恢复44pp；RASP 30%→64%，恢复34pp），\n      说明recovery mechanism非线性。(2) 即使是SOTA importance-based pruning，\n      不考虑CKA信号也会移除GRPO-critical结构。\n      但median档下这个narrative需要nuance：Standard (27%→59%) recovery也不错，\n      说明CKA signal的贡献是incremental而非decisive。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      RASP_20 + Standard_20在5个random seeds下的post-prune GSM8K eval。\n      建立robust方差估计和pairwise significance。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_seed_results: [0.30, 0.28, 0.31, 0.29, 0.32]\n      standard_20_seed_results: [0.27, 0.29, 0.26, 0.28, 0.25]\n      rasp_20_mean: 0.300\n      rasp_20_std: 0.015\n      standard_20_mean: 0.270\n      standard_20_std: 0.016\n      gap_mean_pp: 3.0\n      gap_p_value_paired_t: 0.03\n      gap_p_value_wilcoxon: 0.06\n      seeds_with_gap_lt_2pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义postprune_gap_p_value_5seed为[0.01, 0.08]。取p=0.03 (paired t)。\n      5-seed方差较大：某些seed下gap缩小到<2pp（seed 2: 28% vs 29%，gap为-1pp，\n      Standard actually高于RASP）。这正是median档\"某些seed gap<2pp\"的核心特征。\n      整体mean gap 3pp，paired t-test p=0.03达到conventional significance，\n      但Wilcoxon(更conservative) p=0.06 marginal。Reviewer可以argue either way。\n      Std ~1.5%与GSM8K eval的intrinsic noise一致（N=1319下binomial std ≈ 1.3%）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\"\n        columns: [Seed, RASP_20, Standard_20, \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, \"30.0%\", \"27.0%\", \"+3.0\"]\n          - [123, \"28.0%\", \"29.0%\", \"-1.0\"]\n          - [256, \"31.0%\", \"26.0%\", \"+5.0\"]\n          - [789, \"29.0%\", \"28.0%\", \"+1.0\"]\n          - [1024, \"32.0%\", \"25.0%\", \"+7.0\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"30.0±1.5%\", \"27.0±1.6%\", \"+3.0\"]\n          - [\"p (paired t)\", \"\", \"\", \"0.03\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot showing per-seed accuracy for RASP vs Standard with connecting lines. 一个seed交叉，其余RASP占优。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap在统计边界：paired t p=0.03但一个seed显示反转。\n      这意味着Claim 1必须弱化——不能说\"significantly preserves more reasoning ability\"，\n      而应说\"tends to preserve more\"或\"preserves more on average across seeds\"。\n      但重要的是，recovery后的gap可能比post-prune gap更稳定，\n      因为GRPO amplifies structural advantages。Multi-seed GRPO recovery\n      数据（如果有budget做）会更有说服力。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation (20% Sparsity)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      在20% sparsity下测试不同scoring方法：magnitude-only、gradient-only、\n      random pruning。与RASP和Standard对比，隔离CKA的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.22\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.28\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.05\n      rasp_gsm8k_1319_ref: 0.30\n      standard_gsm8k_1319_ref: 0.27\n      cka_marginal_contribution_vs_gradient: 2\n      cka_marginal_contribution_vs_magnitude: 8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random pruning接近collapse (5%)——随机移除20%结构大概率命中critical components。\n      Magnitude-only (22%)低于gradient-based (28%)因为weight magnitude在Qwen架构\n      中不是结构重要性的good proxy（RMSNorm使magnitude scale less informative）。\n      Gradient-only (28%)接近Standard (27%)是预期的——Standard本身就是gradient-based\n      importance + magnitude的组合。RASP (30%)比gradient-only高2pp，\n      这就是CKA的marginal contribution。Median档下这个2pp差异modest但方向正确。\n      关键insight：CKA的价值不在post-prune accuracy的marginal gain，\n      而在recovery-method-specific的交互效应（plan_009会显示）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Scoring Method Ablation\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Post-Prune GSM8K, \"vs RASP Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP (α=1), \"30.0%\", \"—\"]\n          - [Standard (gradient+magnitude), \"27.0%\", \"-3.0pp\"]\n          - [Gradient-only, \"28.0%\", \"-2.0pp\"]\n          - [Magnitude-only, \"22.0%\", \"-8.0pp\"]\n          - [Random, \"5.0%\", \"-25.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Horizontal bar chart ranking scoring methods by post-prune accuracy. Clear hierarchy: RASP > Gradient ≈ Standard > Magnitude >> Random.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA的post-prune marginal contribution仅2pp (vs gradient-only)，\n      Reviewer会质疑是否值得额外的CKA计算开销。Defense需要两个角度：\n      (1) recovery后gap放大（plan_004数据），(2) interaction效应（plan_009）。\n      Random collapse (5%)提供useful lower bound。\n      Magnitude-only的劣势支持\"importance metric choice matters\"的general argument。\n\n  - name: \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h)与recovery后per-structure\n      activation变化的相关性分析。Mixed-effects regression。\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups_analyzed: 784\n      n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n      cka_beta_coefficient: 0.18\n      cka_beta_p_value: 0.02\n      cka_incremental_r2: 0.08\n      full_model_r2: 0.34\n      weight_norm_beta_p: 0.001\n      gradient_importance_beta_p: 0.008\n      activation_magnitude_beta_p: 0.04\n      cka_weight_norm_correlation: 0.42\n      vif_cka: 2.1\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义CKA beta p在[0.005, 0.05]，incremental R²在[0.05, 0.12]。\n      取p=0.02, incremental R²=8%。CKA显著但effect size中等。\n      关键nuance：weight norm (r=0.42 with CKA)也是significant predictor (p=0.001)，\n      incremental R²比CKA高。VIF=2.1说明共线性moderate但未达alarming levels (>5)。\n      这意味着CKA captures some unique variance (8%)但大部分recoverability\n      被simpler metrics解释。Layer random effect variance=0.06说明层间差异存在\n      但不dominant。Full model R²=0.34意味着66%的方差unexplained——\n      recoverability是complex多因素决定的。\n      Claim 2必须弱化为\"additional predictive signal\"而非\"stronger predictor\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Mixed-Effects Regression (MLP Groups, N=784)\"\n        columns: [Predictor, β, SE, p, \"Incremental R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Weight Norm, 0.31, 0.06, \"<0.001\", \"14%\"]\n          - [Gradient Importance, 0.22, 0.07, \"0.008\", \"11%\"]\n          - [Activation Magnitude, 0.12, 0.06, \"0.04\", \"5%\"]\n          - [CKA F(h), 0.18, 0.07, \"0.02\", \"8%\"]\n          - [\"Layer (random)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"σ²=0.06\"]\n          - [\"Full Model\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"R²=0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-MLP-group F(h) vs recovery accuracy retention, color-coded by layer. Trend visible but noisy. Partial regression plot after controlling for covariates.\"\n      - \"Forest plot showing standardized β coefficients with 95% CI for all predictors.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA provides statistically significant but modest additional signal。\n      Weight norm和gradient importance是stronger individual predictors。\n      共线性(r=0.42)意味着CKA部分captures与weight norm相同的information。\n      论文中需要honest presentation：CKA is not the strongest predictor，\n      但它captures unique variance不被其他metrics覆盖。\n      这支持\"CKA as complementary signal\"的framing而非\"CKA as superior metric\"。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20)，same data budget，\n      SFT-only recovery（no GRPO）。测试recovery method是否改变optimal pruning order。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.57\n      sft_only_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      sft_standard_advantage_pp: 7\n      sft_standard_vs_grpo_standard: \"+5pp\"\n      sft_rasp_vs_grpo_rasp: \"-7pp\"\n      interaction_effect_2x2_anova_p: 0.008\n      interaction_effect_size_eta2: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是median档最强claim的支撑实验。已有N=100数据：sft_rasp_20=57%，\n      sft_standard_20=64%。N=1319预期保持这个pattern。\n      SFT下Standard优于RASP 7pp——方向与GRPO完全相反（GRPO下RASP优5pp）。\n      交叉效应显著(p=0.008)：pruning method × recovery method interaction\n      在2×2 ANOVA中eta²=0.12（medium effect size）。\n      机制解释：SFT通过teacher-forcing扩展correct paths——Standard保留的\n      high-importance结构更适合supervised signal的gradient flow。\n      GRPO通过reward signal压缩incorrect paths——RASP保留的functionally unique\n      结构更好地维持了RLVR exploration的diversity。\n      这个crossover是genuinely novel的发现，且mechanistically interpretable。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Pruning × Recovery Interaction\"\n        columns: [Pruning, SFT-Only, GRPO, \"Δ (GRPO - SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"57.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"+7.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"-5.0pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP - Standard)\", \"-7.0pp\", \"+5.0pp\", \"Interaction: 12pp\"]\n      - name: \"2×2 ANOVA Results\"\n        columns: [Source, F, p, \"η²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Pruning Method, 1.2, 0.28, 0.02]\n          - [Recovery Method, 0.8, 0.38, 0.01]\n          - [\"Pruning × Recovery\", 8.4, 0.008, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot (line chart): x-axis = Recovery Method (SFT, GRPO), y-axis = GSM8K accuracy, two lines (RASP, Standard) crossing. Classic disordinal interaction pattern.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是整篇paper在median档下最clean的result。交叉效应12pp且p<0.01。\n      ANOVA显示main effects均不显著——pruning method和recovery method\n      各自不决定accuracy，但interaction dominates。\n      这直接支持Claim 3：\"recovery method conditions optimal pruning order\"。\n      Narrative pivot到interaction作为核心贡献完全justified。\n      需要注意：这个ANOVA是在N=1319的single eval上做的，\n      严格来说需要multi-seed validation。但effect size足够大(12pp)\n      使reviewer likely接受。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      25% sparsity下的完整pipeline：RASP和Standard prune → eval → SFT → GRPO。\n      测试sparsity level robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k: 0.18\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k: 0.14\n      rasp_25_postprune_gap_pp: 4\n      rasp_25_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.48\n      standard_25_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.55\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.55\n      standard_25_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.48\n      grpo_recovery_gap_25_pp: 7\n      interaction_maintained: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      25% sparsity移除更多结构，post-prune accuracy进一步下降。\n      RASP 18% vs Standard 14%——gap从3pp扩大到4pp因为更多pruning decisions\n      意味着CKA signal有更多机会区分functionally redundant vs unique。\n      Recovery趋势与20%一致但更pronounced：SFT下Standard优7pp (55% vs 48%)，\n      GRPO下RASP优7pp (55% vs 48%)。交互效应维持甚至增强。\n      GRPO recovery gap从5pp扩大到7pp——在higher sparsity下，\n      保留functionally unique结构的优势更明显因为GRPO需要更多structural diversity\n      来maintain exploration。但overall recovery ceiling降低（55% vs 64% at 20%），\n      符合\"more pruning = harder recovery\"的general expectation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Model, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_25, \"18.0%\", \"48.0%\", \"55.0%\"]\n          - [Standard_25, \"14.0%\", \"55.0%\", \"48.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: x-axis = sparsity (20%, 25%), y-axis = post-GRPO accuracy, two lines (RASP, Standard). RASP advantage widens with sparsity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      25%数据强化两个narrative：(1) RASP advantage scales with sparsity，\n      (2) interaction effect is robust across sparsity levels。\n      但overall recovery降低——55% vs 79% dense = 70% retention，\n      接近practical utility threshold。这为30% probe设定预期。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe (Prune + Eval Only)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      30% sparsity下仅prune + eval（不做recovery）。\n      Map sparsity threshold where both methods approach collapse。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k: 0.08\n      standard_30_postprune_gsm8k: 0.03\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.04\n      gap_pp: 5\n      both_near_collapse: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有D005实验在35% sparsity显示collapse。30%接近threshold：\n      RASP勉强维持8%（generation部分functional但reasoning严重受损），\n      Standard接近完全collapse (3%)。Gap扩大到5pp但两者都在near-random水平。\n      EOS rate差异说明RASP保留了basic generation ability而Standard已崩溃。\n      这个数据点重要性在于showing the trend：20% (30/27) → 25% (18/14) → 30% (8/3)，\n      RASP advantage在pp上持续但两者都approaching zero。\n      Recovery at 30%可能仍然possible for RASP but infeasible for Standard——\n      但不做recovery所以这是speculative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Sparsity Scaling\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP Post-Prune, Standard Post-Prune, \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"30.0%\", \"27.0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"18.0%\", \"14.0%\", \"4\"]\n          - [\"30%\", \"8.0%\", \"3.0%\", \"5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard. Both declining, gap widening in absolute pp but both approaching zero.\"\n    analysis: >\n      30%数据展示diminishing returns：虽然RASP gap在pp上扩大，\n      但两者都approaching collapse。This bounds RASP's practical applicability\n      to 20-25% sparsity range for this model。\n      对论文有价值：shows the method's operating range honestly，\n      不oversell到high sparsity。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      Best recovered config (RASP_20 post-GRPO) 在OOD benchmarks上评估。\n      Shows recovery generalizes beyond GSM8K。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_grpo_math500: 0.38\n      standard_grpo_math500: 0.33\n      rasp_grpo_humaneval: 0.42\n      standard_grpo_humaneval: 0.41\n      rasp_grpo_mmlu: 0.55\n      standard_grpo_mmlu: 0.54\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      dense_mmlu: 0.62\n      math500_rasp_advantage_pp: 5\n      humaneval_rasp_advantage_pp: 1\n      mmlu_rasp_advantage_pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义MATH-500上RASP advantage 0-8pp，HumanEval无差异。\n      MATH-500上RASP优5pp (38% vs 33%)——MATH-500与GSM8K同domain (math reasoning)，\n      CKA-aware pruning保留的reasoning structures对math reasoning broadly有效。\n      HumanEval (code)上近乎无差异(1pp)——coding ability依赖不同的structural components，\n      CKA signal对code generation无特异性。MMLU (knowledge)同样无差异——\n      pruning主要影响reasoning而非factual knowledge retrieval。\n      Dense model的retention：MATH-500 73% (38/52)，HumanEval 72% (42/58)，\n      MMLU 89% (55/62)。MMLU retention最高因为knowledge更robust to pruning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, Dense, RASP+GRPO, Standard+GRPO, \"Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GSM8K, \"79.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"+5\"]\n          - [MATH-500, \"52.0%\", \"38.0%\", \"33.0%\", \"+5\"]\n          - [HumanEval, \"58.0%\", \"42.0%\", \"41.0%\", \"+1\"]\n          - [MMLU, \"62.0%\", \"55.0%\", \"54.0%\", \"+1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart or grouped bar: RASP vs Standard across 4 benchmarks. Math-domain advantage clear, non-math negligible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD结果是mixed——这是median档的定义特征。MATH-500优势支持\"reasoning-specific\"\n      narrative但HumanEval/MMLU无差异限制了generalization claim。\n      论文framing需要careful：CKA-aware pruning preserves math reasoning structures\n      specifically，而非general capabilities。这actually strengthens mechanistic story\n      （CKA signal captures reasoning-specific redundancy），但limits practical impact。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning baseline。\n      Lower priority than GRASPrune。\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k: 0.20\n      bonsai_20_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.52\n      bonsai_20_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai是gradient-free方法，与magnitude-only类似但有structural constraints。\n      Post-prune 20%——低于RASP (30%)和Standard (27%)但高于GRASPrune (8%)。\n      Gradient-free意味着它not as targeted但also avoids gradient noise。\n      Recovery到50%——低于RASP (64%)和Standard (59%)。\n      在median档下Bonsai提供another data point但不改变main narrative。\n      其主要价值是showing that even simple methods achieve reasonable recovery，\n      reinforcing \"GRPO is broadly effective\" message。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Added to Table 2 as additional row.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai是completeness baseline。不改变ranking或narrative。\n      如果space tight可以放appendix。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity。\n      验证CKA-based scoring的稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.91\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.93\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.97\n      cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_1024: -0.01\n      cka_compute_time_256: \"8min\"\n      cka_compute_time_512: \"15min\"\n      cka_compute_time_1024: \"28min\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA基于kernel method，inherently对sample size robust。\n      Split-half ρ=0.91 > 0.9 threshold说明scoring是reproducible。\n      256 vs 1024 samples导致accuracy仅差1pp——说明256 samples足够\n      获得near-optimal pruning decision。这支持practical applicability\n      （CKA computation cost可控）。Cal 512→1024的marginal gain minimal (ρ=0.97)，\n      说明diminishing returns。Compute time与sample size近线性。\n      Median档下这些数字都\"okay but not impressive\"——ρ=0.91不是0.98，\n      有些noise在CKA estimation中。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: CKA Stability\"\n        columns: [Calibration Size, \"Rank Corr vs 1024\", Post-Prune Acc, Compute Time]\n        rows:\n          - [256, 0.93, \"29.0%\", \"8 min\"]\n          - [512, 0.97, \"30.0%\", \"15 min\"]\n          - [1024, \"1.00 (ref)\", \"30.0%\", \"28 min\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: calibration size vs rank correlation. Plateau after 512.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA scoring是stable enough for practical use。256 samples提供\n      reasonable trade-off（8min compute, 93% rank preservation）。\n      这addresses reviewer concern about CKA overhead。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} in S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α at 20% sparsity。\n      Post-prune GSM8K eval for each。\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_gsm8k: 0.27\n      alpha_0p25_gsm8k: 0.28\n      alpha_0p5_gsm8k: 0.29\n      alpha_1p0_gsm8k: 0.30\n      alpha_2p0_gsm8k: 0.34\n      alpha_4p0_gsm8k: 0.40\n      optimal_alpha: 4.0\n      optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp: 13\n      curve_shape: \"monotonically increasing but noisy\"\n      alpha_1_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 10\n      seed_sensitivity_at_optimal: \"±3pp across 3 seeds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有初步数据：alpha_ablation_westd_cal256显示α=4.0给出40% accuracy (highest)。\n      α=0等价于importance-only (Standard)，预期27%——与Standard结果一致。\n      α从0到4单调递增说明CKA signal consistently有益。但median档的nuance：\n      曲线噪声较多——α=0.25和α=0.5之间差异仅1pp，可能在noise range内。\n      Optimal α=4.0远高于default α=1——说明CKA signal应该被more heavily weighted，\n      current RASP default (α=1)是suboptimal。13pp gap (α=0 vs α=4)比\n      median档定义的5-10pp范围更大——但这与已有实验数据一致(40% vs 27%)。\n      Seed sensitivity ±3pp at α=4说明optimal point不完全stable——\n      某些seed下α=2可能更好。这limits the precision of α recommendation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: α Ablation\"\n        columns: [α, \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"vs α=0 Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0 (importance-only), \"27.0%\", \"—\"]\n          - [0.25, \"28.0%\", \"+1pp\"]\n          - [0.5, \"29.0%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [1.0, \"30.0%\", \"+3pp\"]\n          - [2.0, \"34.0%\", \"+7pp\"]\n          - [4.0, \"40.0%\", \"+13pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: α vs post-prune accuracy with error bands (3 seeds). Monotonically increasing but wide error bands at higher α.\"\n      - \"Heatmap: α × seed → accuracy. Shows seed-dependent optimal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      α ablation是second practical contribution。Key findings：\n      (1) CKA signal consistently helps (monotonic improvement with α)，\n      (2) default α=1 is suboptimal, α≈2-4 better，\n      (3) but optimal α is seed-sensitive。\n      这suggests adaptive α selection as future work。\n      对Claim 1的影响：RASP with α=4 achieves 40% post-prune (vs Standard 27%)——\n      gap扩大到13pp，比α=1的3pp gap大得多。如果用optimal α，Claim 1显著增强。\n      但需要honest discussion of seed sensitivity和overfitting risk\n      （α是在post-prune accuracy上tuned的，可能不generalize to recovery）。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: >\n      Wall-clock latency + throughput对比：dense、RASP_20、Standard_20。\n      Structured pruning的practical motivation需要efficiency evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 23.8\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 23.5\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n      rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 42.0\n      standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 42.6\n      rasp_speedup_ratio: 1.20\n      standard_speedup_ratio: 1.21\n      rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: \"negligible\"\n      batch_size_tested: [1, 4, 8]\n      speedup_at_batch_8: 1.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义speedup ratio在[1.15, 1.25]。取1.20x for RASP。\n      20% structured sparsity移除20% MLP channel groups——理论speedup上限\n      接近1.25x (MLP占total compute ~67%，移除20% MLP ≈ 13% total reduction)。\n      实际1.20x低于理论上限因为：(1) attention compute不变，\n      (2) memory bandwidth bottleneck at small batch sizes，\n      (3) kernel launch overhead不随width减少。\n      RASP和Standard speedup几乎相同(1.20 vs 1.21)——两者移除相同数量的结构，\n      只是选择了不同的结构。Pruning method不影响inference speed。\n      Batch size 8时speedup略降(1.18x)——更compute-bound时\n      width reduction的relative benefit减少。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Inference Efficiency\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Latency (ms/token)\", Speedup, \"Throughput (tok/s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, 28.5, \"1.00×\", 35.1]\n          - [RASP_20, 23.8, \"1.20×\", 42.0]\n          - [Standard_20, 23.5, \"1.21×\", 42.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: latency comparison at batch sizes 1, 4, 8.\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.20x speedup是modest但real。对于reasoning model的long generation\n      (often 500-2000 tokens)，累积time saving significant。\n      RASP和Standard speedup差异negligible——这是好消息（RASP没有efficiency cost）\n      也是expected（same sparsity level）。\n      论文中作为practical motivation section的supporting data。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: >\n      20% unstructured (magnitude-based) pruning baseline。\n      Calibrate structured vs unstructured gap。\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k: 0.68\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.70\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.62\n      unstructured_20_speedup_ratio: 1.0\n      unstructured_vs_dense_retention_postprune: 0.86\n      unstructured_vs_rasp_structured_postprune_gap: 38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured 20% pruning保留much more accuracy post-prune (68% vs 30% RASP)\n      因为individual weight zeroing far less disruptive than removing entire channel groups。\n      Post-SFT仅微增到70%（already high baseline）。\n      Post-GRPO actually slightly lower (62%)——可能因为sparse weights的gradient flow\n      不如dense结构适合RLVR的exploration-exploitation dynamics。\n      关键：unstructured pruning无法获得real speedup (1.0x)因为sparse operations\n      在standard GPU hardware上不加速。这justifies structured pruning research。\n      Median档预期post_grpo 0.58-0.66，取0.62。\n      GRPO对unstructured model的recovery有限因为post-prune accuracy已经high (68%)，\n      \"ceiling effect\"限制了further improvement，且部分accuracy可能lost\n      to GRPO's exploration noise on already-functional model。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: Structured vs Unstructured\"\n        columns: [Method, Type, Post-Prune, Post-GRPO, Speedup]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, Structured, \"30.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"1.20×\"]\n          - [Standard_20, Structured, \"27.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"1.21×\"]\n          - [Magnitude_20, Unstructured, \"68.0%\", \"62.0%\", \"1.00×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs inference speedup for all methods. Unstructured top-left (high acc, no speedup), structured bottom-right (lower acc, speedup).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unstructured baseline frames the paper's contribution：\n      structured pruning trades post-prune accuracy for real speedup，\n      但needs intelligent structure selection (RASP) and RLVR recovery (GRPO)\n      to close the accuracy gap。RASP+GRPO (64%) approaches unstructured (62%)\n      while delivering 1.20x speedup——this is the practical value proposition。\n      Interesting：RASP+GRPO actually slightly beats unstructured+GRPO (64% vs 62%)。\n      这可能是noise但也可能说明structured pruning creates better GRPO training dynamics。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      SFT-recovered Standard model (64% GSM8K) 在MATH-500和HumanEval上评估。\n      Check if 1%→64% SFT jump is genuine reasoning recovery vs GSM8K memorization。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_standard_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_humaneval: 0.35\n      sft_standard_gsm8k_ref: 0.64\n      sft_rasp_math500: 0.28\n      sft_rasp_humaneval: 0.33\n      sft_rasp_gsm8k_ref: 0.57\n      dense_math500_ref: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval_ref: 0.58\n      math500_retention_standard_sft: 0.58\n      humaneval_retention_standard_sft: 0.60\n    result_rationale: >\n      Standard SFT 64% GSM8K的1%→64%跳跃确实suspicious——但SFT是supervised training，\n      能够快速恢复format和basic arithmetic。MATH-500上30% (vs dense 52%)\n      说明SFT recovery是genuine但partial——不仅是GSM8K pattern memorization，\n      因为MATH-500难度更高，30%仍代表real reasoning能力（random baseline ~5%）。\n      HumanEval 35%同样说明generalized recovery。\n      关键comparison：SFT-Standard MATH-500 (30%) vs GRPO-RASP MATH-500 (38%)——\n      GRPO recovery在OOD上更robust，支持\"RLVR enables deeper recovery\"的argument。\n      但SFT-Standard > SFT-RASP on MATH-500 (30% vs 28%)——\n      SFT recovery maintain Standard's advantage even OOD。Interaction story holds。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: SFT Recovery OOD Check\"\n        columns: [Model, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"79.0%\", \"52.0%\", \"58.0%\"]\n          - [SFT-Standard, \"64.0%\", \"30.0%\", \"35.0%\"]\n          - [SFT-RASP, \"57.0%\", \"28.0%\", \"33.0%\"]\n          - [GRPO-RASP, \"64.0%\", \"38.0%\", \"42.0%\"]\n          - [GRPO-Standard, \"59.0%\", \"33.0%\", \"41.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval retention rates for each recovery condition.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT recovery不是memorization——OOD performance confirms genuine recovery。\n      但GRPO recovery consistently delivers higher OOD retention，\n      especially on MATH-500 (38% vs 30% for best SFT)。\n      This adds to Claim 3：GRPO不仅在GSM8K上favor RASP，\n      在OOD上也delivers deeper、more generalizable recovery。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13171},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02c1e0a5-f063-4cdd-b853-52d47839c413","uuid":"9069e5d4-e511-4062-86ac-dfdb2310de65"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":264763,"duration_api_ms":266128,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Pivot到\"Pruning-Recovery Interaction\"：核心贡献从\"RASP enables recovery\"转为\n  \"pruning method和recovery method之间存在非trivial交互——RLVR和SFT对pruned结构的需求不同\"。\n  Claim 1弱化为\"CKA-aware pruning在GRPO recovery下有中等优势\"；\n  Claim 2保留但降低强度（\"CKA provides additional predictive signal\"而非\"stronger predictor\"）；\n  Claim 3成为最强claim——SFT倾向Standard、GRPO倾向RASP的交叉效应是genuinely novel发现。\n  α优化作为second practical contribution。需要30% sparsity数据展示趋势。\n  竞争力：EMNLP Main有竞争力但需要强writing，Findings高概率。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      对baseline dense模型、RASP_20、Standard_20在完整GSM8K test set (1319 samples)上评估。\n      替代现有N=100的初步数据，获得±2.4pp的tight CI。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_dense_gsm8k_1319: 0.79\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.30\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.27\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 3\n      rasp_ci_95: [0.276, 0.324]\n      standard_ci_95: [0.246, 0.294]\n      gap_p_value_single_seed: 0.11\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=100的reeval_postprune_definitive已显示gap为4pp (31% vs 27% on westb)。\n      扩展到N=1319后，点估计会regress toward mean——N=100的方差大(±9pp CI)，\n      full eval预期RASP 30%、Standard 27%左右。单seed下CI重叠，p≈0.11不显著，\n      这正是median档的核心特征：gap真实存在但需要multi-seed才能确认显著性。\n      Dense baseline 79%与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B已知性能一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Accuracy, \"95% CI\", \"vs Dense Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense Baseline, \"79.0%\", \"[76.8, 81.2]\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"[27.6, 32.4]\", \"-49.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"[24.6, 29.4]\", \"-52.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy for 3 models with error bars (95% CI). Gap between RASP and Standard visible but CI overlap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3pp gap在N=1319下仍不够statistically significant (单seed)。\n      这确认了median档预期：需要multi-seed (plan_006)来建立significance。\n      Post-prune gap本身不是headline claim——recovery后的gap才是。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Recovery)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      对所有recovered模型(SFT→GRPO)在完整GSM8K test set上评估。\n      Paper Table 1的最终数字。\n    expected_results:\n      post_grpo_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      post_grpo_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.59\n      post_sft_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n      post_sft_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      grpo_recovery_gap_pp: 5\n      grpo_rasp_recovery_from_postprune_pp: 34\n      grpo_standard_recovery_from_postprune_pp: 32\n      grpo_rasp_vs_dense_retention: 0.81\n      grpo_standard_vs_dense_retention: 0.75\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义GRPO recovery gap为2-8pp。取中值5pp：RASP 64%、Standard 59%。\n      两者都从post-prune状态大幅恢复（+34pp和+32pp），说明GRPO对两种pruned结构\n      都有效——但RASP保留的functionally unique结构给GRPO多提供了5pp的恢复空间。\n      SFT-only数据(plan_009)会反转这个关系，构成交互效应的核心证据。\n      Recovery gap有限但在N=1319下CI不重叠（64%±2.6 vs 59%±2.7），\n      可达p<0.05显著性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Full Pipeline Results (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [Model, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO, \"Recovery Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"79.0%\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"56.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"+34.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"+32.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO for RASP and Standard. 显示SFT阶段Standard更高，GRPO阶段RASP反超——交叉效应可视化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      关键发现：SFT阶段Standard领先8pp (64% vs 56%)，GRPO阶段RASP反超5pp (64% vs 59%)。\n      这个crossover是Claim 3的核心证据。GRPO gap 5pp虽然modest，但方向一致且N=1319下\n      statistically significant。Narrative pivot到\"pruning-recovery interaction\"合理。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：\n      prune → eval → SFT → GRPO recovery。Primary external baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.08\n      grasp_20_postprune_eos_rate: 0.05\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.42\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.52\n      grasp_sft_recovery_pp: 34\n      grasp_grpo_recovery_from_sft_pp: 10\n      grasp_vs_rasp_grpo_gap_pp: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有初步数据：grasp_baseline_westd显示50-sample post-prune accuracy仅8%，\n      EOS rate 2%，avg_len 4019——与Standard_20的initial状态类似（generation崩溃）。\n      Median档预期GRASPrune post-prune远差于RASP (8% vs 31%)因为GRASPrune\n      优化budgeted importance但不考虑functional redundancy，会移除functionally\n      unique的结构。SFT恢复到42%（从8%有大幅提升，说明结构本身没有完全损坏，\n      只是generation能力崩溃）。GRPO进一步恢复到52%，但仍低于RASP的64%。\n      关键：GRASPrune+GRPO (52%) vs Standard+GRPO (59%)的gap说明\n      pruning method确实影响recovery ceiling，且GRASPrune的\"better importance scoring\"\n      不能弥补missing CKA signal。但GRASPrune+GRPO也在恢复（不是完全fail），\n      这符合median档\"GRPO broadly effective\"的假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Method, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"30.0%\", \"56.0%\", \"64.0%\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"27.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\"]\n          - [GRASPrune_20, \"8.0%\", \"42.0%\", \"52.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三组柱状图对比三种pruning方法的pipeline轨迹。GRASPrune post-prune最差但GRPO recovery可观——说明recovery能力不完全由post-prune accuracy决定。\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune作为baseline提供两个关键insight：(1) post-prune accuracy不能直接预测\n      recovery ceiling（GRASPrune 8%→52%，恢复44pp；RASP 30%→64%，恢复34pp），\n      说明recovery mechanism非线性。(2) 即使是SOTA importance-based pruning，\n      不考虑CKA信号也会移除GRPO-critical结构。\n      但median档下这个narrative需要nuance：Standard (27%→59%) recovery也不错，\n      说明CKA signal的贡献是incremental而非decisive。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      RASP_20 + Standard_20在5个random seeds下的post-prune GSM8K eval。\n      建立robust方差估计和pairwise significance。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_seed_results: [0.30, 0.28, 0.31, 0.29, 0.32]\n      standard_20_seed_results: [0.27, 0.29, 0.26, 0.28, 0.25]\n      rasp_20_mean: 0.300\n      rasp_20_std: 0.015\n      standard_20_mean: 0.270\n      standard_20_std: 0.016\n      gap_mean_pp: 3.0\n      gap_p_value_paired_t: 0.03\n      gap_p_value_wilcoxon: 0.06\n      seeds_with_gap_lt_2pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义postprune_gap_p_value_5seed为[0.01, 0.08]。取p=0.03 (paired t)。\n      5-seed方差较大：某些seed下gap缩小到<2pp（seed 2: 28% vs 29%，gap为-1pp，\n      Standard actually高于RASP）。这正是median档\"某些seed gap<2pp\"的核心特征。\n      整体mean gap 3pp，paired t-test p=0.03达到conventional significance，\n      但Wilcoxon(更conservative) p=0.06 marginal。Reviewer可以argue either way。\n      Std ~1.5%与GSM8K eval的intrinsic noise一致（N=1319下binomial std ≈ 1.3%）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\"\n        columns: [Seed, RASP_20, Standard_20, \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, \"30.0%\", \"27.0%\", \"+3.0\"]\n          - [123, \"28.0%\", \"29.0%\", \"-1.0\"]\n          - [256, \"31.0%\", \"26.0%\", \"+5.0\"]\n          - [789, \"29.0%\", \"28.0%\", \"+1.0\"]\n          - [1024, \"32.0%\", \"25.0%\", \"+7.0\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"30.0±1.5%\", \"27.0±1.6%\", \"+3.0\"]\n          - [\"p (paired t)\", \"\", \"\", \"0.03\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot showing per-seed accuracy for RASP vs Standard with connecting lines. 一个seed交叉，其余RASP占优。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap在统计边界：paired t p=0.03但一个seed显示反转。\n      这意味着Claim 1必须弱化——不能说\"significantly preserves more reasoning ability\"，\n      而应说\"tends to preserve more\"或\"preserves more on average across seeds\"。\n      但重要的是，recovery后的gap可能比post-prune gap更稳定，\n      因为GRPO amplifies structural advantages。Multi-seed GRPO recovery\n      数据（如果有budget做）会更有说服力。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation (20% Sparsity)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      在20% sparsity下测试不同scoring方法：magnitude-only、gradient-only、\n      random pruning。与RASP和Standard对比，隔离CKA的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.22\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.28\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.05\n      rasp_gsm8k_1319_ref: 0.30\n      standard_gsm8k_1319_ref: 0.27\n      cka_marginal_contribution_vs_gradient: 2\n      cka_marginal_contribution_vs_magnitude: 8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random pruning接近collapse (5%)——随机移除20%结构大概率命中critical components。\n      Magnitude-only (22%)低于gradient-based (28%)因为weight magnitude在Qwen架构\n      中不是结构重要性的good proxy（RMSNorm使magnitude scale less informative）。\n      Gradient-only (28%)接近Standard (27%)是预期的——Standard本身就是gradient-based\n      importance + magnitude的组合。RASP (30%)比gradient-only高2pp，\n      这就是CKA的marginal contribution。Median档下这个2pp差异modest但方向正确。\n      关键insight：CKA的价值不在post-prune accuracy的marginal gain，\n      而在recovery-method-specific的交互效应（plan_009会显示）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Scoring Method Ablation\"\n        columns: [Scoring, Post-Prune GSM8K, \"vs RASP Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP (α=1), \"30.0%\", \"—\"]\n          - [Standard (gradient+magnitude), \"27.0%\", \"-3.0pp\"]\n          - [Gradient-only, \"28.0%\", \"-2.0pp\"]\n          - [Magnitude-only, \"22.0%\", \"-8.0pp\"]\n          - [Random, \"5.0%\", \"-25.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Horizontal bar chart ranking scoring methods by post-prune accuracy. Clear hierarchy: RASP > Gradient ≈ Standard > Magnitude >> Random.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA的post-prune marginal contribution仅2pp (vs gradient-only)，\n      Reviewer会质疑是否值得额外的CKA计算开销。Defense需要两个角度：\n      (1) recovery后gap放大（plan_004数据），(2) interaction效应（plan_009）。\n      Random collapse (5%)提供useful lower bound。\n      Magnitude-only的劣势支持\"importance metric choice matters\"的general argument。\n\n  - name: \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h)与recovery后per-structure\n      activation变化的相关性分析。Mixed-effects regression。\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups_analyzed: 784\n      n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n      cka_beta_coefficient: 0.18\n      cka_beta_p_value: 0.02\n      cka_incremental_r2: 0.08\n      full_model_r2: 0.34\n      weight_norm_beta_p: 0.001\n      gradient_importance_beta_p: 0.008\n      activation_magnitude_beta_p: 0.04\n      cka_weight_norm_correlation: 0.42\n      vif_cka: 2.1\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义CKA beta p在[0.005, 0.05]，incremental R²在[0.05, 0.12]。\n      取p=0.02, incremental R²=8%。CKA显著但effect size中等。\n      关键nuance：weight norm (r=0.42 with CKA)也是significant predictor (p=0.001)，\n      incremental R²比CKA高。VIF=2.1说明共线性moderate但未达alarming levels (>5)。\n      这意味着CKA captures some unique variance (8%)但大部分recoverability\n      被simpler metrics解释。Layer random effect variance=0.06说明层间差异存在\n      但不dominant。Full model R²=0.34意味着66%的方差unexplained——\n      recoverability是complex多因素决定的。\n      Claim 2必须弱化为\"additional predictive signal\"而非\"stronger predictor\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Mixed-Effects Regression (MLP Groups, N=784)\"\n        columns: [Predictor, β, SE, p, \"Incremental R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Weight Norm, 0.31, 0.06, \"<0.001\", \"14%\"]\n          - [Gradient Importance, 0.22, 0.07, \"0.008\", \"11%\"]\n          - [Activation Magnitude, 0.12, 0.06, \"0.04\", \"5%\"]\n          - [CKA F(h), 0.18, 0.07, \"0.02\", \"8%\"]\n          - [\"Layer (random)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"σ²=0.06\"]\n          - [\"Full Model\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"R²=0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-MLP-group F(h) vs recovery accuracy retention, color-coded by layer. Trend visible but noisy. Partial regression plot after controlling for covariates.\"\n      - \"Forest plot showing standardized β coefficients with 95% CI for all predictors.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA provides statistically significant but modest additional signal。\n      Weight norm和gradient importance是stronger individual predictors。\n      共线性(r=0.42)意味着CKA部分captures与weight norm相同的information。\n      论文中需要honest presentation：CKA is not the strongest predictor，\n      但它captures unique variance不被其他metrics覆盖。\n      这支持\"CKA as complementary signal\"的framing而非\"CKA as superior metric\"。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20)，same data budget，\n      SFT-only recovery（no GRPO）。测试recovery method是否改变optimal pruning order。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp_gsm8k_1319: 0.57\n      sft_only_standard_gsm8k_1319: 0.64\n      sft_standard_advantage_pp: 7\n      sft_standard_vs_grpo_standard: \"+5pp\"\n      sft_rasp_vs_grpo_rasp: \"-7pp\"\n      interaction_effect_2x2_anova_p: 0.008\n      interaction_effect_size_eta2: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是median档最强claim的支撑实验。已有N=100数据：sft_rasp_20=57%，\n      sft_standard_20=64%。N=1319预期保持这个pattern。\n      SFT下Standard优于RASP 7pp——方向与GRPO完全相反（GRPO下RASP优5pp）。\n      交叉效应显著(p=0.008)：pruning method × recovery method interaction\n      在2×2 ANOVA中eta²=0.12（medium effect size）。\n      机制解释：SFT通过teacher-forcing扩展correct paths——Standard保留的\n      high-importance结构更适合supervised signal的gradient flow。\n      GRPO通过reward signal压缩incorrect paths——RASP保留的functionally unique\n      结构更好地维持了RLVR exploration的diversity。\n      这个crossover是genuinely novel的发现，且mechanistically interpretable。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Pruning × Recovery Interaction\"\n        columns: [Pruning, SFT-Only, GRPO, \"Δ (GRPO - SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, \"57.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"+7.0pp\"]\n          - [Standard_20, \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"-5.0pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP - Standard)\", \"-7.0pp\", \"+5.0pp\", \"Interaction: 12pp\"]\n      - name: \"2×2 ANOVA Results\"\n        columns: [Source, F, p, \"η²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Pruning Method, 1.2, 0.28, 0.02]\n          - [Recovery Method, 0.8, 0.38, 0.01]\n          - [\"Pruning × Recovery\", 8.4, 0.008, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot (line chart): x-axis = Recovery Method (SFT, GRPO), y-axis = GSM8K accuracy, two lines (RASP, Standard) crossing. Classic disordinal interaction pattern.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是整篇paper在median档下最clean的result。交叉效应12pp且p<0.01。\n      ANOVA显示main effects均不显著——pruning method和recovery method\n      各自不决定accuracy，但interaction dominates。\n      这直接支持Claim 3：\"recovery method conditions optimal pruning order\"。\n      Narrative pivot到interaction作为核心贡献完全justified。\n      需要注意：这个ANOVA是在N=1319的single eval上做的，\n      严格来说需要multi-seed validation。但effect size足够大(12pp)\n      使reviewer likely接受。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      25% sparsity下的完整pipeline：RASP和Standard prune → eval → SFT → GRPO。\n      测试sparsity level robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k: 0.18\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k: 0.14\n      rasp_25_postprune_gap_pp: 4\n      rasp_25_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.48\n      standard_25_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.55\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.55\n      standard_25_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.48\n      grpo_recovery_gap_25_pp: 7\n      interaction_maintained: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      25% sparsity移除更多结构，post-prune accuracy进一步下降。\n      RASP 18% vs Standard 14%——gap从3pp扩大到4pp因为更多pruning decisions\n      意味着CKA signal有更多机会区分functionally redundant vs unique。\n      Recovery趋势与20%一致但更pronounced：SFT下Standard优7pp (55% vs 48%)，\n      GRPO下RASP优7pp (55% vs 48%)。交互效应维持甚至增强。\n      GRPO recovery gap从5pp扩大到7pp——在higher sparsity下，\n      保留functionally unique结构的优势更明显因为GRPO需要更多structural diversity\n      来maintain exploration。但overall recovery ceiling降低（55% vs 64% at 20%），\n      符合\"more pruning = harder recovery\"的general expectation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\"\n        columns: [Model, Post-Prune, Post-SFT, Post-GRPO]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_25, \"18.0%\", \"48.0%\", \"55.0%\"]\n          - [Standard_25, \"14.0%\", \"55.0%\", \"48.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: x-axis = sparsity (20%, 25%), y-axis = post-GRPO accuracy, two lines (RASP, Standard). RASP advantage widens with sparsity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      25%数据强化两个narrative：(1) RASP advantage scales with sparsity，\n      (2) interaction effect is robust across sparsity levels。\n      但overall recovery降低——55% vs 79% dense = 70% retention，\n      接近practical utility threshold。这为30% probe设定预期。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe (Prune + Eval Only)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      30% sparsity下仅prune + eval（不做recovery）。\n      Map sparsity threshold where both methods approach collapse。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k: 0.08\n      standard_30_postprune_gsm8k: 0.03\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.04\n      gap_pp: 5\n      both_near_collapse: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有D005实验在35% sparsity显示collapse。30%接近threshold：\n      RASP勉强维持8%（generation部分functional但reasoning严重受损），\n      Standard接近完全collapse (3%)。Gap扩大到5pp但两者都在near-random水平。\n      EOS rate差异说明RASP保留了basic generation ability而Standard已崩溃。\n      这个数据点重要性在于showing the trend：20% (30/27) → 25% (18/14) → 30% (8/3)，\n      RASP advantage在pp上持续但两者都approaching zero。\n      Recovery at 30%可能仍然possible for RASP but infeasible for Standard——\n      但不做recovery所以这是speculative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Sparsity Scaling\"\n        columns: [Sparsity, RASP Post-Prune, Standard Post-Prune, \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"20%\", \"30.0%\", \"27.0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"25%\", \"18.0%\", \"14.0%\", \"4\"]\n          - [\"30%\", \"8.0%\", \"3.0%\", \"5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard. Both declining, gap widening in absolute pp but both approaching zero.\"\n    analysis: >\n      30%数据展示diminishing returns：虽然RASP gap在pp上扩大，\n      但两者都approaching collapse。This bounds RASP's practical applicability\n      to 20-25% sparsity range for this model。\n      对论文有价值：shows the method's operating range honestly，\n      不oversell到high sparsity。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      Best recovered config (RASP_20 post-GRPO) 在OOD benchmarks上评估。\n      Shows recovery generalizes beyond GSM8K。\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_grpo_math500: 0.38\n      standard_grpo_math500: 0.33\n      rasp_grpo_humaneval: 0.42\n      standard_grpo_humaneval: 0.41\n      rasp_grpo_mmlu: 0.55\n      standard_grpo_mmlu: 0.54\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      dense_mmlu: 0.62\n      math500_rasp_advantage_pp: 5\n      humaneval_rasp_advantage_pp: 1\n      mmlu_rasp_advantage_pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义MATH-500上RASP advantage 0-8pp，HumanEval无差异。\n      MATH-500上RASP优5pp (38% vs 33%)——MATH-500与GSM8K同domain (math reasoning)，\n      CKA-aware pruning保留的reasoning structures对math reasoning broadly有效。\n      HumanEval (code)上近乎无差异(1pp)——coding ability依赖不同的structural components，\n      CKA signal对code generation无特异性。MMLU (knowledge)同样无差异——\n      pruning主要影响reasoning而非factual knowledge retrieval。\n      Dense model的retention：MATH-500 73% (38/52)，HumanEval 72% (42/58)，\n      MMLU 89% (55/62)。MMLU retention最高因为knowledge更robust to pruning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, Dense, RASP+GRPO, Standard+GRPO, \"Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GSM8K, \"79.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"+5\"]\n          - [MATH-500, \"52.0%\", \"38.0%\", \"33.0%\", \"+5\"]\n          - [HumanEval, \"58.0%\", \"42.0%\", \"41.0%\", \"+1\"]\n          - [MMLU, \"62.0%\", \"55.0%\", \"54.0%\", \"+1\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart or grouped bar: RASP vs Standard across 4 benchmarks. Math-domain advantage clear, non-math negligible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD结果是mixed——这是median档的定义特征。MATH-500优势支持\"reasoning-specific\"\n      narrative但HumanEval/MMLU无差异限制了generalization claim。\n      论文framing需要careful：CKA-aware pruning preserves math reasoning structures\n      specifically，而非general capabilities。这actually strengthens mechanistic story\n      （CKA signal captures reasoning-specific redundancy），但limits practical impact。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning baseline。\n      Lower priority than GRASPrune。\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k: 0.20\n      bonsai_20_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.52\n      bonsai_20_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai是gradient-free方法，与magnitude-only类似但有structural constraints。\n      Post-prune 20%——低于RASP (30%)和Standard (27%)但高于GRASPrune (8%)。\n      Gradient-free意味着它not as targeted但also avoids gradient noise。\n      Recovery到50%——低于RASP (64%)和Standard (59%)。\n      在median档下Bonsai提供another data point但不改变main narrative。\n      其主要价值是showing that even simple methods achieve reasonable recovery，\n      reinforcing \"GRPO is broadly effective\" message。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Added to Table 2 as additional row.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai是completeness baseline。不改变ranking或narrative。\n      如果space tight可以放appendix。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity。\n      验证CKA-based scoring的稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.91\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.93\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.97\n      cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_1024: -0.01\n      cka_compute_time_256: \"8min\"\n      cka_compute_time_512: \"15min\"\n      cka_compute_time_1024: \"28min\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA基于kernel method，inherently对sample size robust。\n      Split-half ρ=0.91 > 0.9 threshold说明scoring是reproducible。\n      256 vs 1024 samples导致accuracy仅差1pp——说明256 samples足够\n      获得near-optimal pruning decision。这支持practical applicability\n      （CKA computation cost可控）。Cal 512→1024的marginal gain minimal (ρ=0.97)，\n      说明diminishing returns。Compute time与sample size近线性。\n      Median档下这些数字都\"okay but not impressive\"——ρ=0.91不是0.98，\n      有些noise在CKA estimation中。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: CKA Stability\"\n        columns: [Calibration Size, \"Rank Corr vs 1024\", Post-Prune Acc, Compute Time]\n        rows:\n          - [256, 0.93, \"29.0%\", \"8 min\"]\n          - [512, 0.97, \"30.0%\", \"15 min\"]\n          - [1024, \"1.00 (ref)\", \"30.0%\", \"28 min\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: calibration size vs rank correlation. Plateau after 512.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA scoring是stable enough for practical use。256 samples提供\n      reasonable trade-off（8min compute, 93% rank preservation）。\n      这addresses reviewer concern about CKA overhead。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} in S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α at 20% sparsity。\n      Post-prune GSM8K eval for each。\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_gsm8k: 0.27\n      alpha_0p25_gsm8k: 0.28\n      alpha_0p5_gsm8k: 0.29\n      alpha_1p0_gsm8k: 0.30\n      alpha_2p0_gsm8k: 0.34\n      alpha_4p0_gsm8k: 0.40\n      optimal_alpha: 4.0\n      optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp: 13\n      curve_shape: \"monotonically increasing but noisy\"\n      alpha_1_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 10\n      seed_sensitivity_at_optimal: \"±3pp across 3 seeds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有初步数据：alpha_ablation_westd_cal256显示α=4.0给出40% accuracy (highest)。\n      α=0等价于importance-only (Standard)，预期27%——与Standard结果一致。\n      α从0到4单调递增说明CKA signal consistently有益。但median档的nuance：\n      曲线噪声较多——α=0.25和α=0.5之间差异仅1pp，可能在noise range内。\n      Optimal α=4.0远高于default α=1——说明CKA signal应该被more heavily weighted，\n      current RASP default (α=1)是suboptimal。13pp gap (α=0 vs α=4)比\n      median档定义的5-10pp范围更大——但这与已有实验数据一致(40% vs 27%)。\n      Seed sensitivity ±3pp at α=4说明optimal point不完全stable——\n      某些seed下α=2可能更好。这limits the precision of α recommendation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: α Ablation\"\n        columns: [α, \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"vs α=0 Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0 (importance-only), \"27.0%\", \"—\"]\n          - [0.25, \"28.0%\", \"+1pp\"]\n          - [0.5, \"29.0%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [1.0, \"30.0%\", \"+3pp\"]\n          - [2.0, \"34.0%\", \"+7pp\"]\n          - [4.0, \"40.0%\", \"+13pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: α vs post-prune accuracy with error bands (3 seeds). Monotonically increasing but wide error bands at higher α.\"\n      - \"Heatmap: α × seed → accuracy. Shows seed-dependent optimal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      α ablation是second practical contribution。Key findings：\n      (1) CKA signal consistently helps (monotonic improvement with α)，\n      (2) default α=1 is suboptimal, α≈2-4 better，\n      (3) but optimal α is seed-sensitive。\n      这suggests adaptive α selection as future work。\n      对Claim 1的影响：RASP with α=4 achieves 40% post-prune (vs Standard 27%)——\n      gap扩大到13pp，比α=1的3pp gap大得多。如果用optimal α，Claim 1显著增强。\n      但需要honest discussion of seed sensitivity和overfitting risk\n      （α是在post-prune accuracy上tuned的，可能不generalize to recovery）。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: >\n      Wall-clock latency + throughput对比：dense、RASP_20、Standard_20。\n      Structured pruning的practical motivation需要efficiency evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 23.8\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 23.5\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n      rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 42.0\n      standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 42.6\n      rasp_speedup_ratio: 1.20\n      standard_speedup_ratio: 1.21\n      rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: \"negligible\"\n      batch_size_tested: [1, 4, 8]\n      speedup_at_batch_8: 1.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档定义speedup ratio在[1.15, 1.25]。取1.20x for RASP。\n      20% structured sparsity移除20% MLP channel groups——理论speedup上限\n      接近1.25x (MLP占total compute ~67%，移除20% MLP ≈ 13% total reduction)。\n      实际1.20x低于理论上限因为：(1) attention compute不变，\n      (2) memory bandwidth bottleneck at small batch sizes，\n      (3) kernel launch overhead不随width减少。\n      RASP和Standard speedup几乎相同(1.20 vs 1.21)——两者移除相同数量的结构，\n      只是选择了不同的结构。Pruning method不影响inference speed。\n      Batch size 8时speedup略降(1.18x)——更compute-bound时\n      width reduction的relative benefit减少。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Inference Efficiency\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Latency (ms/token)\", Speedup, \"Throughput (tok/s)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, 28.5, \"1.00×\", 35.1]\n          - [RASP_20, 23.8, \"1.20×\", 42.0]\n          - [Standard_20, 23.5, \"1.21×\", 42.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: latency comparison at batch sizes 1, 4, 8.\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.20x speedup是modest但real。对于reasoning model的long generation\n      (often 500-2000 tokens)，累积time saving significant。\n      RASP和Standard speedup差异negligible——这是好消息（RASP没有efficiency cost）\n      也是expected（same sparsity level）。\n      论文中作为practical motivation section的supporting data。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: >\n      20% unstructured (magnitude-based) pruning baseline。\n      Calibrate structured vs unstructured gap。\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k: 0.68\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_gsm8k: 0.70\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_gsm8k: 0.62\n      unstructured_20_speedup_ratio: 1.0\n      unstructured_vs_dense_retention_postprune: 0.86\n      unstructured_vs_rasp_structured_postprune_gap: 38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured 20% pruning保留much more accuracy post-prune (68% vs 30% RASP)\n      因为individual weight zeroing far less disruptive than removing entire channel groups。\n      Post-SFT仅微增到70%（already high baseline）。\n      Post-GRPO actually slightly lower (62%)——可能因为sparse weights的gradient flow\n      不如dense结构适合RLVR的exploration-exploitation dynamics。\n      关键：unstructured pruning无法获得real speedup (1.0x)因为sparse operations\n      在standard GPU hardware上不加速。这justifies structured pruning research。\n      Median档预期post_grpo 0.58-0.66，取0.62。\n      GRPO对unstructured model的recovery有限因为post-prune accuracy已经high (68%)，\n      \"ceiling effect\"限制了further improvement，且部分accuracy可能lost\n      to GRPO's exploration noise on already-functional model。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: Structured vs Unstructured\"\n        columns: [Method, Type, Post-Prune, Post-GRPO, Speedup]\n        rows:\n          - [RASP_20, Structured, \"30.0%\", \"64.0%\", \"1.20×\"]\n          - [Standard_20, Structured, \"27.0%\", \"59.0%\", \"1.21×\"]\n          - [Magnitude_20, Unstructured, \"68.0%\", \"62.0%\", \"1.00×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs inference speedup for all methods. Unstructured top-left (high acc, no speedup), structured bottom-right (lower acc, speedup).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unstructured baseline frames the paper's contribution：\n      structured pruning trades post-prune accuracy for real speedup，\n      但needs intelligent structure selection (RASP) and RLVR recovery (GRPO)\n      to close the accuracy gap。RASP+GRPO (64%) approaches unstructured (62%)\n      while delivering 1.20x speedup——this is the practical value proposition。\n      Interesting：RASP+GRPO actually slightly beats unstructured+GRPO (64% vs 62%)。\n      这可能是noise但也可能说明structured pruning creates better GRPO training dynamics。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      SFT-recovered Standard model (64% GSM8K) 在MATH-500和HumanEval上评估。\n      Check if 1%→64% SFT jump is genuine reasoning recovery vs GSM8K memorization。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_standard_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_humaneval: 0.35\n      sft_standard_gsm8k_ref: 0.64\n      sft_rasp_math500: 0.28\n      sft_rasp_humaneval: 0.33\n      sft_rasp_gsm8k_ref: 0.57\n      dense_math500_ref: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval_ref: 0.58\n      math500_retention_standard_sft: 0.58\n      humaneval_retention_standard_sft: 0.60\n    result_rationale: >\n      Standard SFT 64% GSM8K的1%→64%跳跃确实suspicious——但SFT是supervised training，\n      能够快速恢复format和basic arithmetic。MATH-500上30% (vs dense 52%)\n      说明SFT recovery是genuine但partial——不仅是GSM8K pattern memorization，\n      因为MATH-500难度更高，30%仍代表real reasoning能力（random baseline ~5%）。\n      HumanEval 35%同样说明generalized recovery。\n      关键comparison：SFT-Standard MATH-500 (30%) vs GRPO-RASP MATH-500 (38%)——\n      GRPO recovery在OOD上更robust，支持\"RLVR enables deeper recovery\"的argument。\n      但SFT-Standard > SFT-RASP on MATH-500 (30% vs 28%)——\n      SFT recovery maintain Standard's advantage even OOD。Interaction story holds。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: SFT Recovery OOD Check\"\n        columns: [Model, GSM8K, MATH-500, HumanEval]\n        rows:\n          - [Dense, \"79.0%\", \"52.0%\", \"58.0%\"]\n          - [SFT-Standard, \"64.0%\", \"30.0%\", \"35.0%\"]\n          - [SFT-RASP, \"57.0%\", \"28.0%\", \"33.0%\"]\n          - [GRPO-RASP, \"64.0%\", \"38.0%\", \"42.0%\"]\n          - [GRPO-Standard, \"59.0%\", \"33.0%\", \"41.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval retention rates for each recovery condition.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT recovery不是memorization——OOD performance confirms genuine recovery。\n      但GRPO recovery consistently delivers higher OOD retention，\n      especially on MATH-500 (38% vs 30% for best SFT)。\n      This adds to Claim 3：GRPO不仅在GSM8K上favor RASP，\n      在OOD上也delivers deeper、more generalizable recovery。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"02c1e0a5-f063-4cdd-b853-52d47839c413","total_cost_usd":0.43490325,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13171,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":13537,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13171,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13537,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13171},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8129,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008229,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13537,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13171,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.42667425000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"4e9f3c7e-0849-4b97-975e-2ac9825d549c"}
